{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two cattle</b> — corresponding to Moses and Aaron, who made peace between Israel and their Father in heaven." "<b>Rams, lambs, goats</b> — three species, corresponding to priests, Levites, and Israelites, and corresponding to Torah, Prophets, and Writings." "<b>עתודים</b> — plene with vav. David, who descended from him (Naḥshon), was blessed with six blessings. And עתודים is nothing but an expression of standing, as you say: אשר התעתדו לגל, and it says: ועתדה בשדה לך. Meaning: the son of Naḥshon will come with six attributes and will lay the foundation of the Temple. Another matter: וקרבנו — why the extra vav? Corresponding to six things that were taken from the first Adam and are destined to return when the son of Naḥshon, who is the Messiah, comes. And these are the six things taken from the first Adam: His radiance — as it is written: משנה פניו ותשלחהו. His life — as it is written: כי עפר אתה ואל עפר תשוב. His stature — as it is written: ויתחבא האדם — teaches that his stature was diminished and became one hundred cubits. The fruits of the earth and the tree — as it is written: ארורה האדמה בעבורך בעצבון תאכלנה. The luminaries — as it is written: וחפרה הלבנה ובושה החמה. And from where that He stored them away? As it is said: וימנע מרשעים אורם. And from where that they are destined to return in the days of the Messiah? As it is said: ואוהביו כצאת השמש בגבורתו. His life — as it is written: כי כימי העץ ימי עמי — five hundred years, the trunk of a sycamore, five hundred years. His stature — as it is written: ואולך אתכם קוממיות — in upright stature. The fruits of the earth and the tree — as it is written: הגפן תתן פריה והארץ תתן יבולה. The luminaries — as it is written: והיה אור הלבנה כאור החמה ואור החמה יהיה שבעתים."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "The phrase ואין עתודים אלא לשון עמידה introduces an etymology treating עתודים as related to עמידה (standing); the two prooftexts cited (אשר התעתדו לגל and ועתדה בשדה לך) are rendered here without translation as the Hebrew forms are essential to the wordplay."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:38.391385413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}